      "writtenOn": "2026-10-02T12:58:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`crossDomainPathComputation` stays `true` once any earlier k-path was hybrid. Consider `k\u003d0` hybrid and `k\u003d1` a valid OpenROADM path: the regular branch sets `shortestPathAtoZ` and breaks, but this block still runs. It can return `false` at line 333 and throw away the valid path, or it launches TAPI path computations that aren\u0027t needed.\n\nWhen the TAPI step does succeed, the result is never written to `pceResult` or `shortestPathAtoZ`, so `calcPath` returns the stale status.\n\nI suggest skipping this block when `shortestPathAtoZ !\u003d null`.",
      "revId": "905d8c753d07892543a8dec6354f68b09b7ef12f",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
    {
