      "writtenOn": "2026-10-02T12:58:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`setIs2ndStepHybrid(true)` is never called. The constructor of `PathComputationServiceImpl` sets it to `false`, and nothing changes it. The path computation launched from here therefore runs as a normal one, and the `!hybridPath \u0026\u0026 isSecondStepHybridPC` branch at line 221 is never taken. The same applies to `setNpathOrder(nporder)`.\n\nRather than adding the missing static setter calls, I suggest passing `isSecondStepHybrid` and `npathorder` along with the path computation request that `PceCrossDomainOrchestrator.performPCE` sends. `PceSendingPceRPCs` already takes both as constructor arguments. Only the step from `PathComputationServiceImpl` goes through static fields, which concurrent requests would overwrite (see my comment on 125823 about global mutable state).\n\nFor example, an overload in `PathComputationService`:\n\n```\nListenableFuture\u003cPathComputationRequestOutput\u003e pathComputationRequest(\n        PathComputationRequestInput input,\n        boolean isSecondStepHybrid,\n        int npathorder);\n```\n\nThe existing `pathComputationRequest(input)` would delegate with `false, 0`, and `performPCE` would call the overload with `true, nporder`.",
      "revId": "905d8c753d07892543a8dec6354f68b09b7ef12f",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
