      "writtenOn": "2026-10-02T12:58:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`getInstance(null, null)` creates the singleton with `null` services if it runs before `CrossDomainServiceOrchestrator` is activated. That can happen if a request arrives early or in a unit test without OSGi. Later calls to `getInstance(pcs, nps)` ignore their arguments, so the `null` services stay cached, and `pcs.pathComputationRequest` / `nps.putNotification` throw an NPE.\n\nAlso, `CrossDomainServiceOrchestrator.close()` never resets the instance. After a bundle restart, the stale services are kept.\n\nI suggest a getter that fails fast when no instance exists, and clearing the instance in `close()`. Better still, inject the orchestrator into its users.",
      "revId": "905d8c753d07892543a8dec6354f68b09b7ef12f",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
