      "writtenOn": "2026-10-02T12:58:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This loop isn\u0027t a timeout:\n\n- It\u0027s a busy-spin of 10M iterations, which finishes in a few milliseconds while keeping a PCE thread at 100% CPU. The TAPI PCE answers asynchronously, typically after hundreds of milliseconds or more.\n- `isSecondStepSuccessfullyFinished` and `isSecondStepAborted` aren\u0027t `volatile`. The JIT may hoist the reads, and then the loop never sees the update.\n- `isSecondStepAborted` has no setter, so `getHasSecondStepFailed()` is always false.\n- After a success (line 372), the outer loop still goes on to launch a path computation for the next k.\n\nI suggest waiting on the result directly, for example with a `CompletableFuture` that the callback completes, and `get(timeout, TimeUnit.SECONDS)`. Then `break` on success. For example:\n\n```\n// Pcro2ndStepCallback\nprivate final CompletableFuture\u003cBoolean\u003e result \u003d new CompletableFuture\u003c\u003e();\n\npublic void onSuccess(PathComputationRequestOutput response) {\n    ...\n    result.complete(isResponseOk(response));\n}\n\npublic void onFailure(Throwable cause) {\n    ...\n    result.complete(false);\n}\n\n// PceGraph\ntry {\n    if (callback.result.get(30, TimeUnit.SECONDS)) {\n        break;\n    }\n} catch (TimeoutException | ExecutionException e) {\n    LOG.warn(\"PC on TAPI Domain failed or timed out for the Kpath order \u003d {}\", \n              korder, e);\n} catch (InterruptedException e) {\n    Thread.currentThread().interrupt();\n    break;\n}\n```",
      "revId": "905d8c753d07892543a8dec6354f68b09b7ef12f",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
